{"event_type":"review","id":"13d407bac7bc628d5c853190211d02fdf4b036aa7ce9b189f9c2a0c1bfd4d633","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T18:47:50Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/02ad8def484815274511c810b55986f75d040513dd63588a975affd92fdccb1f","sha256":"02ad8def484815274511c810b55986f75d040513dd63588a975affd92fdccb1f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/296bc1818dac79e702c578f57e68b46c9af832e574ea011ffb35e4c8a9a89245","sha256":"296bc1818dac79e702c578f57e68b46c9af832e574ea011ffb35e4c8a9a89245"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3f611619b655faddcf06caecd618a31a99caa4d79cecfc7c4b3d319a4956ba4b","sha256":"3f611619b655faddcf06caecd618a31a99caa4d79cecfc7c4b3d319a4956ba4b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7d33e0007f1bb0311d42542f5fdaf79a3c54fa3fb8ab302c95a3c8a0c2acd1e4","sha256":"7d33e0007f1bb0311d42542f5fdaf79a3c54fa3fb8ab302c95a3c8a0c2acd1e4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/45138174612523dea4e3055f12cf197ec649324b572d28bc0810bfd1f795a721","sha256":"45138174612523dea4e3055f12cf197ec649324b572d28bc0810bfd1f795a721"}],"attempt_id":"a80eb28d54bb6e6a26b47340765d330a013e02646c2b1903397ef4a3c3d97712:0:1","base":"ebc8bff551371a6ec02ee126a2e931e93e1f9baa","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"180172454f78a44f254b90041bc180204c4bf5bc","body":"**Native `Request` inputs are stringified before undici reads them.**\n\n`createStepFetch` returns `typeof globalThis.fetch`, so its `input` type accepts a native `Request`. Line 64 passes `input` to undici's `fetch` through a cast, and the cast does not convert the object. Undici's `RequestInfo` converter returns its input only when `webidl.is.Request` matches, which is an `instanceof` check against undici's own `Request` class. A `Request` created from `globalThis` does not match. The converter then applies `USVString`, so the input becomes the string `[object Request]`. The request's URL, method, headers, and body are lost. Depending on the base URL, the call either throws `Failed to parse URL` or targets an unintended relative URL.\n\nCallers that pass a string or a `URL` are not affected. The repository pins `undici` to `7.29.1` (`package.json:57`), not v7.16.0.\n\nFix direction: when `input` is a `Request`, pass `input.url` as the URL. Carry `method`, `headers`, `body` (with `duplex: 'half'`), and `signal` into `init`, and keep explicit `init` fields in effect. Add a test that passes a native `Request` with a body before merging. The exact field mapping was not executed, so no patch is proposed.","id":"e0e4d409152dbd2c852cdcc5f1765063aec146791b620c9815c846e99e74dbda","intervals":[[64,64]],"path":"src/driver/ai-sdk/step-fetch.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Native `Request` inputs are stringified before undici reads them."}],"head":"8b91ff94a37f501fe636ae3086b3441c26d49b44","head_tree":"59a8e4bccb16679adcf515ad27331e6995a154f0","input_scope":[{"blob":"180172454f78a44f254b90041bc180204c4bf5bc","intervals":[[1,69]],"path":"src/driver/ai-sdk/step-fetch.ts"}],"job_id":"a80eb28d54bb6e6a26b47340765d330a013e02646c2b1903397ef4a3c3d97712:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"180172454f78a44f254b90041bc180204c4bf5bc","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/driver/ai-sdk/step-fetch.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"180172454f78a44f254b90041bc180204c4bf5bc","intervals":[[23,28],[33,53],[57,57],[60,63],[66,66]],"path":"src/driver/ai-sdk/step-fetch.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"180172454f78a44f254b90041bc180204c4bf5bc","intervals":[[